theory.intro:
A composite solid is made by joining simple solids, such as a cylinder standing on a rectangular prism. Its surface area is the total of every outside face.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.5]
\draw (0,0)--(6,0);
\draw (6,0)--(6,4);
\draw (6,4)--(0,4);
\draw (0,4)--(0,0);
\draw (6,0)--(8.5981,1.5);
\draw (8.5981,1.5)--(8.5981,5.5);
\draw (8.5981,5.5)--(6,4);
\draw (0,4)--(2.299,5.327316);
\draw (6.299,5.5)--(8.5981,5.5);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(2.5981,1.5);
\draw[dashed] (2.5981,1.5)--(8.5981,1.5);
\draw[dashed] (2.5981,1.5)--(2.5981,4.434366);
\draw (2.299,4.75) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=2,y radius=0.6];
\draw[dashed] (2.299,4.75) arc[start angle=180,end angle=0,x radius=2,y radius=0.6];
\draw (2.299,4.75)--(2.299,9.75);
\draw (6.299,4.75)--(6.299,9.75);
\path (6.299,7.25) node[anchor=west,xshift=5pt,draw=none,fill=none] {$h$};
