workedExamples.question_text:
A closed cylinder of radius $2$ cm and height $7$ cm sits centrally on a rectangular prism measuring $9$ cm by $6$ cm by $3$ cm high. The cylinder's whole base touches the prism. Find the total surface area of the combined solid, correct to $2$ decimal places.

The plan shows where the solids meet.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (9,6);
\draw (4.5,3) circle (2);
\fill (4.5,3) circle (1.2pt);
\draw (4.5,3)--(6.5,3);
\path (5.5,3) node[above] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (4.5,0) node[below] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (9,3) node[right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A cube of side length $2$ cm sits on a rectangular prism measuring $10$ cm by $7$ cm by $4$ cm high. The cube's whole bottom face touches the prism. Find the total surface area of the combined solid.

The front elevation shows the arrangement; the prism extends $7$ cm from front to back. The diagram is schematic.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (10,4);
\draw (4,4)--(4,6)--(6,6)--(6,4);
\path (5,0) node[below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\path (10,2) node[right] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (5,6) node[above] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A closed cylindrical monument of radius $1$ m and height $3$ m sits centrally on a square concrete block of side length $5$ m and height $2$ m. The cylinder's whole base touches the block. Every outside surface except the block's bottom is painted. Painting costs $\$8$ per square metre. Find the cost, correct to the nearest cent.

The plan shows the contact circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,5);
\draw (2.5,2.5) circle (1);
\fill (2.5,2.5) circle (1.2pt);
\draw (2.5,2.5)--(3.5,2.5);
\path (3,2.5) node[above] {$1\text{ m}$};
\path (2.5,0) node[below] {$5\text{ m}$};
\path (5,2.5) node[right] {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

